Subject: [PATCH] fix(valve): bind `rating` before use in _execute_legacy

`Valve._execute_legacy` reads a bare `rating` that is never bound in the
function, so every legacy-CSV valve that is neither knife nor pinch raises
`NameError: name 'rating' is not defined` instead of building.

The two branches immediately above it already do the right thing with
`fp.PRating.lower()`; this binds that once and uses it consistently.

Reproduced with Quetzal 1.8.9 (76cc1a62788898e732b908465fe42d7e9f220d5d) —
`pCmd.makeValve(...)` on any ball/globe/generic rating.

Upstream: https://github.com/sargo-devel/Quetzal   (not yet submitted)

--- a/pFeatures.py
+++ b/pFeatures.py
@@ -2523,10 +2523,11 @@
     def _execute_legacy(self, fp, H):
-        if fp.PRating.lower().find("knife") + 1:
+        rating = fp.PRating.lower()
+        if rating.find("knife") + 1:
             self._execute_knife_gate(fp, H)
             return
-        if fp.PRating.lower().find("pinch") + 1:
+        if rating.find("pinch") + 1:
             self._execute_pinch(fp, H)
             return
 
